<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/7th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle of Baekgang</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">663</span> · <a href="/centuries/7th-century">7th century</a> · Also known as Battle of Hakusukinoe, Battle of Baekgang-gu</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle of Baekgang was fought in 663 near the mouth of the Geum river in south-western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/korea">Korea</a> between Tang Chinese and Silla forces and the fleet of Yamato <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/japan">Japan</a>, sent to support the Baekje restoration movement. The Tang navy destroyed the Japanese fleet, ending hopes of reviving Baekje. Fearing invasion, Japan built defensive fortresses and strengthened its central state.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-baekgang.jpg" alt="Battle of Baekgang" width="320" height="414" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Stillskywkpd · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Map_of_the_Battle_of_Baekgang.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
